: 0, "impression_count": 195, "like_count": 7, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Data centres could drive sodium-ion, LDES adoption in Europe – analyst #energysky -- via Energy Storage News: https://t.co/oPhvIDBtjh", "url": "https://x.com/SolarFred/status/2116644509865980227"}, {"author_id": "564053183", "created_at": "2026-11-01T20:30:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116991178956566536"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Sodium-ion batteries are moving into electric vehicles and grid storage. But can the emerging technology compete with lithium-ion in 2026?", "display_url": "bit.ly/4A44eLn", "end": 111, "expanded_url": "https://bit.ly/4A44eLn", "images": [{"height": 1080, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116991183247364096/0NQ05aEE?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1920}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116991183247364096/0NQ05aEE?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 88, "status": 200, "title": "Sodium-ion vs. lithium-ion: Tracking the battery race in 2026", "unwound_url": "https://interestingengineering.com/energy/sodium-ion-vs-lithium-ion-batteries-2026?utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=social&utm_content=1793555866", "url": "https://t.co/VIkOC4v055"}]}, "id": "2116991178956566536", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1009, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "In 2026, lithium-ion batteries dominate the market, but sodium-ion is gaining momentum. https://t.co/VIkOC4v055", "url": "https://x.com/IntEngineering/status/2116991178956566536"}, {"author_id": "1778567374448545792", "created_at": "2026-11-01T15:02:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116908721892982925"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "mp.weixin.qq.com/s/l00Vtguvm5v4…", "end": 124, "expanded_url": "https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/l00Vtguvm5v42Rc6tAjZlg", "start": 101, "unwound_url": "https://mp.weixin.qq.com/mp/wappoc_appmsgcaptcha?poc_token=HH9U52qjntWW8kfOAipvVPkDOfocpjvvk7X7SQ15&target_url=https%3A%2F%2Fmp.weixin.qq.com%2Fs%2Fl00Vtguvm5v42Rc6tAjZlg", "url": "https://t.co/eMZ6BhidBT"}]}, "id": "2116908721892982925", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "3 GWh! INTILION and CATL Sign Strategic Agreement, Taking Sodium-Ion Energy Storage Global at Scale.\nhttps://t.co/eMZ6BhidBT", "url": "https://x.com/netzerolucas/status/2116908721892982925"}, {"author_id": "132816632", "created_at": "2026-10-31T14:44:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116541866350985308", "2116556162317287877"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 8, "start": 1, "tag": "Sodium"}, {"end": 43, "start": 35, "tag": "lithium"}], "urls": [{"description": "Sodium-ion was supposed to replace lithium-ion. Instead, it may be learning to live alongside it. CATL’s Naxtra sodium-ion cells have reached approximately 175 Wh/kg, still below the ~205 Wh/kg benchmark for LFP. Yet commercial momentum is building, including a 3-year, 60 GWh energy storage agreement, with domestic deliveries planned for September 2026 and global deliveries expected from June 2027. Why does sodium-ion matter? Reduced dependence on lithium, strong low-temperature performance, and greater supply-chain diversification. For stationary storage, energy density is generally less critical than system cost, operating performance, and lifetime economics. But challenges remain. Sodium-ion manufacturing capacity is still small compared with lithium-ion, while supply chains and cost competitiveness need further development. According to the IEA, promising near-term applications include cold-climate markets, selected stationary storage applications, and hybrid sodium-lithium systems", "display_url": "lnkd.in/p/ddhPeH2Z", "end": 133, "expanded_url": "https://lnkd.in/p/ddhPeH2Z", "images": [{"height": 512, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116541869400178688/TZimsi9-?format=jpg&name